Any system that is running on the OS, and can communicate on the network is host.

Network protocols, ensure that different computer systems, using different hardware and different software
can communicate with each other.  ----- Standard form of cummunication

Cummunication between different hosts, via protocol is transferred/facilitated throught the use of packets. (数据包)

The primary goal of networking is the exchage of information betwenn networked hosts. 
This information is transferred by packets. (Network Packets)

数据包以电力，更准确说是比特流(二进制中的0和1)，通过以太网或是无线网的方式在光纤中进行物理传播。（物理传输）

The structure of any protocols: 1. Header; 2. Payload(有效载荷);
Header: The packet that containing important information, for instead, where do the packets are coming on (source),
their destination or etc... It has a protocol-based-specific structure that ensures any hosts can correctly handle 
the overall communication.
Payload: The actual data that's been sent, such email, messages, contents etc...

OSI(Open Systems Interconnection) model is a conceptual framework. (概念框架)
OSI model just be as the way of understanding how does the network work.
7. Application Layer --> HTTP, FTP, SSH, DNS
6. Presentation Layer --> SSL/TLS, SSH
5. Session Layer --> APIs, NetBios, RPC
4. Transport Layer --> TCP, UDP
3. Network Layer --> IP, ICMP
2. Data link Layer --> Ethernet, switches , routers
